<title>USA: Motorola wins $6 mln contract in Russia.</title>
<headline>Motorola wins $6 mln contract in Russia.</headline>
<dateline>ARLINGTON HEIGHTS, Ill. 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Motorola Inc said Tuesday its international cellular infrastructure group won a $6 million contract to deploy Advanced Mobile Phone Service and Narrowband Advanced Mobile Phone Service cellular systems in Novosibirsk, Russia.</p>
<p>Gene O'Rourke, senior director of emerging markets for Motorola cellular infrastructure group, said deployment of the company's cellular system strengthens its commitment to meeting Russia's telecommunications infrastructure development.</p>
<p>	     ((Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787))</p>
